==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|tolmetsche}}. Compare Proto-Slavic {{m|sla-pro|*tъlmačь||interpreter}} (Russian {{m|ru|sc=Cyrl|толма́ч}}, Polish {{m|pl|tłumacz}}), borrowed from a {{etyl|trk|de}} language, from Proto-Turkic {{m|trk-pro|*tilmaç}} ({{cog|tr|dilmaç||translator, interpreter}}; {{m|tr|dil}}, Azeri {{m|az|dil}}).

